.TH AGENTOSCTL 1 "October 2026" "AgentOS 0.1.0" "AgentOS manual"
.SH NAME
agentosctl \- control the AgentOS agent-native operating environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agentosctl
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agentosctl
is the operator and user interface to AgentOS. It is a thin client: every
state-changing command is sent to the AgentOS core service over a Unix domain
socket, and the service is what enforces policy and writes the audit trail.
.PP
The commands that work without the service \(em
.BR doctor ,
.BR config ,
and
.BR runtime
\(em exist so that an installation whose service will not start can still be
diagnosed.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-socket \fIPATH\fR
Core IPC socket. Default: \fI/run/agentos/core.sock\fR, or \fB$AGENTOS_SOCKET\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON instead of human-readable text.
.TP
.B \-\-timeout \fISECONDS\fR
Per-request deadline. Default: 30.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS doctor
Diagnose the installation from local facts only: configuration validity, service
reachability, runtime availability, the Node.js requirement for the DSH runtime,
the credential file's permissions, and the loaded policy. Exits non-zero when a
finding of severity \fIerror\fR is present.
.SS health
Report service, database, runtime, task, and approval health.
.SS task
.TP
.B task run \fIPROMPT\fR [\-\-runtime \fIID\fR] [\-\-level-cap \fIP0..P3\fR] [\-\-priority \fIN\fR] [\-\-watch]
Submit a prompt as a task. The privilege cap defaults to \fBP0\fR and bounds the
authority the task may ever reach, independently of policy.
.TP
.B task list [\-\-state \fISTATE\fR] [\-\-limit \fIN\fR] [\-\-all-owners]
List tasks. Only the superuser may list another owner's tasks.
.TP
.B task show \fITASK_ID\fR
Show one task.
.TP
.B task history \fITASK_ID\fR
Show a task's event history, including every policy decision.
.TP
.B task cancel \fITASK_ID\fR
Request cancellation. A queued task is cancelled immediately; a running task is
asked to stop.
.TP
.B task watch \fITASK_ID\fR [\-\-timeout \fISECONDS\fR]
Follow a task until it settles or asks for an approval.
.SS approval
.TP
.B approval list [\-\-state \fISTATE\fR]
List approvals.
.TP
.B approval show \fIAPPROVAL_ID\fR
Show one approval with its bound parameters, parameter digest, and the plain
statement of its effect.
.TP
.B approval request \fITASK_ID\fR \fIOPERATION\fR \-\-target \fITARGET\fR [\-\-reason \fITEXT\fR] [\-\-ttl \fISECONDS\fR]
Create an approval request. The policy engine refuses an operation it would
never permit, so no approval prompt exists for an impossible action.
.TP
.B approval grant \fIAPPROVAL_ID\fR [\-\-note \fITEXT\fR]
Authorize the operation. Prints the single-use nonce bound to the target and
parameter set.
.TP
.B approval deny \fIAPPROVAL_ID\fR [\-\-note \fITEXT\fR]
Refuse the operation.
.TP
.B approval revoke \fIAPPROVAL_ID\fR
Revoke a granted approval that has not been used.
.SS policy
.TP
.B policy inventory
List every declared tool with its privilege level, whether it needs an approval,
and the rule that governs it.
.TP
.B policy evaluate \fITOOL\fR [\-\-params \fIJSON\fR] [\-\-task-id \fIID\fR]
Evaluate a proposed tool call without running it. Exits non-zero when the
decision is not \fIallow\fR.
.SS audit
.TP
.B audit query [\-\-task-id \fIID\fR] [\-\-kind \fIKIND\fR] [\-\-operation \fINAME\fR] [\-\-since \fITIMESTAMP\fR] [\-\-limit \fIN\fR]
Query the audit trail, newest first.
.TP
.B audit summary
Show audit counts by kind and outcome.
.SS system
.TP
.B system snapshot
CPU, memory, swap, filesystem capacity, and the highest-CPU processes.
.TP
.B system processes [\-\-limit \fIN\fR] [\-\-sort cpu|memory|pid] [\-\-min-cpu \fIPERCENT\fR]
List processes from /proc.
.TP
.B system disks
Filesystem capacity and inode use.
.TP
.B system services [\-\-state failed|running|all]
List systemd units.
.TP
.B system service \fIUNIT\fR
Show one unit's state.
.TP
.B system logs [\-\-unit \fIUNIT\fR] [\-\-lines \fIN\fR] [\-\-priority \fI0..7\fR] [\-\-since \fIEXPR\fR]
Read bounded journal entries.
.TP
.B system read \fITOOL\fR [\-\-params \fIJSON\fR]
Run a read-only System Bridge tool by name.
.SS events
.TP
.B events recent [\-\-limit \fIN\fR]
Print recent events.
.TP
.B events follow [\-\-timeout \fISECONDS\fR]
Follow the event stream. A timeout of 0 means never stop.
.SS config
.TP
.B config show
Print the effective configuration as JSON, with no credential material.
.TP
.B config render
Print the package default configuration document.
.TP
.B config path
Print the files that contribute to the effective configuration, in application
order.
.SS runtime
.TP
.B runtime list
List the shipped runtimes.
.TP
.B runtime probe [\fIRUNTIME_ID\fR]
Report one runtime's availability and its capability set.
.SS demo
Run the keyless end-to-end flow against the live service: task creation, a
runtime turn, a policy decision, an approval request, a refusal, and the audit
trail. Requires no model credential and no network.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/agentos/agentos.toml
Package-managed configuration; replaced on upgrade.
.TP
.I /etc/agentos/agentos.local.toml
Administrator overrides; never replaced by a package.
.TP
.I /etc/agentos/policies/
Policy documents, applied in lexical order.
.TP
.I /etc/agentos/credentials.env
Model credentials. Mode \fB0600\fR, root-owned. A package never installs this
file and never prints its contents.
.TP
.I /var/lib/agentos/agentos.sqlite3
Tasks, approvals, task history, and the audit trail.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AGENTOS_SOCKET
Overrides the default core socket path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.TP
.B 3
The operation was denied by policy, or the caller lacks access.
.TP
.B 4
The core service or the runtime is unavailable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR gnome-extensions (1)
.PP
Documentation: https://github.com/agentos-project/agentos
